-# Sanity Clean Content Studio
+# Fit content Studio
@@ -3 +3,2 @@
-Congratulations, you have now installed the Sanity Content Studio, an open-source real-time content editing environment connected to the Sanity backend.
+Standalone Sanity Studio for Fit app (`quli96gc`), private dataset `production`.
+Keep this directory beside `../fit-app`; do not embed it in the app.
@@ -5 +6,7 @@ Congratulations, you have now installed the Sanity Content Studio, an open-sourc
-Now you can do the following things:
+```sh
+npm install
+npm run dev
+npm run typegen
+npm run build
+npx sanity schemas deploy
+```
@@ -7,3 +14,19 @@ Now you can do the following things:
-- [Read “getting started” in the docs](https://www.sanity.io/docs/introduction/getting-started?utm_source=readme)
-- [Join the Sanity community](https://www.sanity.io/community/join?utm_source=readme)
-- [Extend and build plugins](https://www.sanity.io/docs/content-studio/extending?utm_source=readme)
+The Studio models candidate profiles/evidence, job opportunities, application
+questions and answers, fit report versions, cover letters, company research,
+interview briefs, fit assessments, site/CV pages and writing guidance.
+
+Only **Analysis settings** has been populated, using the current code prompts and
+candidate context at the owner's request. Edit its three tabs and Publish to
+change enabled analysis tasks. Other content types remain empty. Do not import
+jobs or artifacts automatically. The app's content storage remains active until
+a later, verified cutover. See `../fit-app/docs/analysis-settings.md` for activation.
+Sanity generates ordinary document IDs; relationships use references. Original
+app IDs have dedicated fields for future migration and permalink preservation.
+
+`npm run typegen` extracts the schema and scans queries in
+`../fit-app/lib/sanity/`, generating types in that app. Commit the generated types
+with app changes so app builds do not require this sibling checkout.
+
+The local Studio uses your Sanity account. The app uses its own read-only token,
+stored in its ignored `.env.local`; no app token belongs in Studio code.
+See `../fit-app/docs/sanity-content.md` for source mapping and the cutover plan.
